Detect Linux aarch64 as arm64 in cmake/TargetArch.cmake

On Linux aarch64, TargetArch.cmake matched __aarch64__ inside the 32-bit
ARM block and emitted "arm" instead of "arm64". CMakeLists.txt only
enables HPX_WITH_GENERIC_CONTEXT_COROUTINES automatically for "riscv64"
and "arm64", leaving it OFF on Linux aarch64 and failing to compile
libs/core/coroutines/src/swapcontext.cpp with the x86-only #error.

Emit "arm64" for __arm64__ and __aarch64__ before the 32-bit ARM branch,
matching the macOS arm64 path in the same file.

Author: Rohit Goswami <rgoswami@ieee.org>
--- hpx-1.11.0/cmake/TargetArch.cmake.orig	2025-06-29 14:43:20.000000000 +0000
+++ hpx-1.11.0/cmake/TargetArch.cmake	2026-11-19 12:15:00.000000000 +0000
@@ -17,7 +17,9 @@
 
 set(archdetect_cpp_code
     "
-    #if defined(__arm__) || defined(__TARGET_ARCH_ARM) || defined(__arm64__) || defined(__aarch64__)
+    #if defined(__arm64__) || defined(__aarch64__)
+        #error cmake_ARCH arm64
+    #elif defined(__arm__) || defined(__TARGET_ARCH_ARM)
         #if defined(__ARM_ARCH_7__) \\
             || defined(__ARM_ARCH_7A__) \\
             || defined(__ARM_ARCH_7R__) \\
